# Commands run by the launchd job com.redwood.demo (see com.redwood.demo.plist).
# The network, when the kernel has one (QEMU: run-ios.sh QEMU_NET=1, virtio_net=1): en0 configured by configd's
# IPConfiguration over DHCP and stored as the primary service, which is what tells iOS it is connected (Safari
# said "not connected to the Internet" without it). Without en0 it says "no such interface"; in the background,
# so its wait for an address holds nothing up.
/redwood/bin/net_test dhcp en0 waitaddr en0 40 store &
